# AssistU2Win — App Screen Design (not website pages)

Every Assist U2 Win screen must feel like a **native, full-screen operating app** — an AI-powered real estate command center — not a marketing site, landing page, or generic CRM dashboard.

For **dashboard and in-app workspace screens**, this rule overrides generic “website dashboard” or slate/emerald marketing defaults in other rules; page-level ombre backgrounds still follow `assistu2win-midnight-ombre-canvas.mdc`.

## Product feel

| Target | Avoid |
|--------|--------|
| AI-powered real estate operating system | Marketing website |
| Dense, operational command UI | Hero sections, brochure spacing |
| Card-based app panels | Generic multi-column website dashboards |
| Real data + premium empty states | Fake seed/demo database rows |

## Global shell (required on app screens)

- **Full-screen app shell** with `min-h-dvh`, `overflow-x-hidden` — no horizontal scroll.
- **Compact operational spacing** — tight section gaps; no landing-page vertical padding.
- **Desktop (lg+):** sticky **left app rail** (~240px) + center workspace + optional right panel (e.g. AI assistant).
- **Mobile / tablet:** single column; **fixed bottom nav** with safe bottom padding on main content (`pb-28` or equivalent).
- Reuse shared primitives from `@/components/dashboard/AgentCommandShell` when building dashboard-family screens (`APP_SHELL_BG`, `APP_GRID`, `PAGE_CONTAINER`, `AppRail`, `BottomAppNav`, `CARD_NORMAL`, `CARD_FEATURED`, `PANEL`).

Responsive breakpoints: **mobile → tablet (md) → laptop/desktop (lg+)**. Use `min-w-0` on grid children so content does not force overflow.

## Layout anti-patterns

- No landing-page hero blocks (`text-4xl` headlines, marketing subcopy, full-viewport empty space).
- No generic website dashboard chrome (wide marketing nav, brochure sidebars, telemetry-style “matrix” pages unless explicitly scoped).
- No uncontrolled cyan glow; use **controlled** edge glow on featured panels only (see `CARD_FEATURED` in `AgentCommandShell`).
- Do not scatter one-off shell layouts per page — extend the shared shell pattern.

## Color system (app chrome & panels)

Use these for **shell surfaces, panels, borders, and text** on app screens (complements `assistu2win-midnight-ombre-canvas` for page-level ombre backgrounds in `app/globals.css`):

| Role | Hex |
|------|-----|
| Background | `#080C1A`, `#0B1020`, `#050713` |
| Panels | `#111827`, `#161C31` |
| Borders | `#1E2A44` |
| Accent | `#00F2FE` |
| Muted text | `#94A3B8` |
| Primary text | `#F8FAFC` |

Prefer exporting repeated class strings from `AgentCommandShell` (or shared tokens) over duplicating long Tailwind hex strings across files.

## Data & empty states

- **Use real data** from existing hooks, server components, and Supabase-backed flows where available.
- When data is unavailable, show **premium empty states** (clear label, one action, muted helper line) — never insert fake database rows or mock buyer lists.
- Loading: inline skeletons or compact spinners inside panels — not full-page marketing loaders.

## Route awareness

- Leads analytics app screen: **`/dashboard/leads/analytics`** (`AnalyticsStudioView`).
- Do not treat **`/dashboard/analytics`** (legacy telemetry page) as the target for new app-shell analytics work unless explicitly requested.

## Hard boundaries (do not change unless user asks)

- APIs, auth flows, Supabase schema/migrations, RLS, `proxy.ts`, and **intake pages**.
- Follow `assistu2win-core.mdc` for real-estate terminology and forbidden B2B vocabulary on user-facing copy.

## Reference implementation

- Home command: `app/dashboard/page.tsx`
- Shared shell: `components/dashboard/AgentCommandShell.tsx`
- Analytics app screen: `components/leads/analytics/AnalyticsStudioView.tsx` + `app/dashboard/leads/analytics/page.tsx`
